CORE
main.py
--unwind 30
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The "is a plain numeral" test guarding int(s, base) is folded for a constant
s. Before, it stayed symbolic, so the parsed bound could be any value and
the unwinding assertion failed (and real programs unwound every loop it
bounded to the limit).
